TOTK: Optimizer.RemoveNode (as in Ryujinx) follows a removed node's sources into their producers and strips the producers'
own sources' use lists once a source has no uses left, so the next dead code pass removes the chain feeding it. A producer
with more than one destination keeps the others in use: here it is followed only when every destination is unused. An
Ampere HMMA is one operation with two (Rd and Rd + 1); in OoT's NDVE upscaler (4f41ccf24f163e0d) the last
one's Rd + 1 is overwritten unread, and removing that copy took the lane, the block, the LDS, LDSM and MOVM results and
the 45 HMMAs before it out of the module, so the one left read uninitialised values (dashes over the title movie and the
3D frame). A single-destination producer is followed as before; TotK's 3,763 compared jobs are byte-identical.

--- a/src/Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader/Translation/Optimizations/Optimizer.cs
+++ b/src/Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader/Translation/Optimizations/Optimizer.cs
@@ -390,7 +390,11 @@ namespace Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader.Translation.Optimizations
                         // result is unused, so its sources are still live: stripping their use lists here made the next
                         // DCE pass delete the whole chain feeding a global-memory atomic turned into a helper call, which
                         // then read an uninitialised value (TOTK's sun-visibility kernel; our c7830fac lost its atomicMin).
-                        if (!HasSideEffects(src.AsgOp))
+                        // TOTK (2026-11-06): nor into one with another destination still in use. An Ampere HMMA is one operation
+                        // with two (Rd, Rd + 1); in OoT's upscaler (4f41ccf24f163e0d) the last one's Rd + 1 is
+                        // overwritten unread, removing that copy stripped the HMMA's sources, and the next pass deleted the lane,
+                        // the block and the 45 HMMAs before it, leaving it to read uninitialised values.
+                        if (!HasSideEffects(src.AsgOp) && DestHasNoUses(src.AsgOp))
                         {
                             nodes.Enqueue(src.AsgOp);
                         }
